# Public age recipients only. One age1... key per line (multiple allowed).
# This file is a TEMPLATE. Scripts refuse to use recipients.example as a live
# recipients file — copy it to recipients.local (gitignored) after you:
#   1. Generate a real age keypair (private key stays with the operator)
#   2. Run an isolated restore rehearsal that decrypts with that identity
#   3. Record the restore proof before enabling CI/schedule
#
# Generate a real pair:
#   age-keygen -o ~/secure/palpitae-backup.identity
#   age-keygen -y ~/secure/palpitae-backup.identity > scripts/backup/recipients.local
#   chmod 600 ~/secure/palpitae-backup.identity scripts/backup/recipients.local
#
# Optional second recipient (recovery operator):
#   age-keygen -y ~/secure/palpitae-backup-recovery.identity >> scripts/backup/recipients.local
#
# Never commit AGE-SECRET-KEY lines.
# Never paste orphan/example public keys — generate your own with age-keygen.
#
# After the steps above, recipients.local should contain one or more lines like:
#   age1...
